From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:32:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/30] Add a manual e2e that runs the LayerFS spike image as a
 microVM actor

Run the LayerFS spike image on a pool with guestDevices: [fuse] and on a
pool without it, to measure the FUSE-backed layer store in a microVM
actor. The test lives outside internal/e2e/suites, so the normal e2e
lanes do not run it. The layerfs-e2e workflow runs it on a kind cluster
when a pull request gets the layerfs-e2e label, or by hand, and writes
the timings to the job summary.

Fork-Topic: layerfs-e2e
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
